19ad7adf4" commit="f03a1e05863e242ad680dfce9ae5c27f477f006c" commit_message="finalize: make sure virtual dev is off before in-place wiping  For in-place wiping, we cut-off device immediately after wiping without additional reboot. However, crossystem disable_dev_request=1 requires reboot to save the flag into flash on some device. Immediately cut-off causes the flag corrupt and device will not leave dev mode.  This CL add a check. For factory process, finalize will fail if virtual dev is on. For RMA, reboot is used instead of cut-off.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51846 TEST=Run finalize on Chell with virtual dev sw on/off.  Change-Id: I0fb8347e50941c95f60d3edb45fed5419ad7adf4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/336610 Commit-Ready: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="336610" owner_email="shunhsingou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/10/336610/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie7b662a3fb4ab84d55e547d18a574f1d1341805f" commit="181d8b4d6125b3f966c16156e965cfbc67b4bbb5" commit_message="goofy: Revise documentation for touch events.  The description for touch settings were slightly confusing in previous version.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:30239,chrome-os-partner:50847 TEST=make test; manually started touchscreen_wrap test.  Change-Id: Ie7b662a3fb4ab84d55e547d18a574f1d1341805f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/337471 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="337471" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumo